# Netlify routing for the static Mintlify export.
#
# Mintlify emits sidebar links WITHOUT a trailing slash (/getting-started/
# prerequisites), but the export writes each page to <route>/index.html. On
# Netlify a directory-style path without the slash is answered with a 301 to
# the slashed form, and that redirect breaks the client-side transition -- so
# every sidebar click looked like a full page reload.
#
# These are rewrites (status 200), not redirects: the page is served directly
# at the URL Mintlify linked to, so no navigation is interrupted.
#
# Generated from docs.json's navigation -- one line per page. Regenerate this
# file when the navigation changes, or new pages start 301ing again.

